        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, thank you for referring your 78-year-old male patient, admitted on 18/12/2007 with an acute exacerbation of known COPD. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Clinical examination confirmed bilateral expiratory wheezing. Chest X-ray showed pulmonary hyperinflation without signs of pneumonia. Arterial blood gas analysis revealed mild hypoxaemia with hypercapnia. Blood tests showed mild inflammatory markers. The patient was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and close monitoring of vital signs and oxygen saturation. He responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. He is discharged on an optimised inhaler regimen and a short oral steroid course. Please arrange follow-up within two weeks. Do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
